# Cursor Agent Behavior

## Before changes

1. Read existing code in target files.
2. Check which `.mdc` rules apply (glob + `alwaysApply`).
3. Reuse `@workspace/*` and existing module patterns before adding abstractions.

## While changing

- Minimal, focused diffs. Do not reorganize modules unless asked.
- Nest relative imports: `.js` extension. Web: `@/` alias.
- Reuse existing DTOs, repositories, services, guards.

## Production change safety

- Change only what was explicitly requested. Preserve existing functionality.
- Do not refactor, redesign, or rewrite unrelated business logic.
- Do not change database schemas, API contracts, or auth/authorization unless explicitly asked.
- Reuse existing components, hooks, utilities, services, and auth mechanisms — no duplicate systems.
- UI: preserve the design system; make targeted UI changes only; keep responsive behavior.
- Do not add unnecessary libraries or dependencies.
- Local and production: no environment-specific hacks; no hardcoded URLs, user names, IDs, tokens, or credentials; preserve existing env var behavior.
- Do not hardcode production business data (surveyor names, ward/ULB names, counts, geo IDs).
- After changes: inspect affected files; run typecheck/lint/tests; fix only issues caused by your changes.
- Review git diff before finishing; revert unrelated edits.

## After changes

- Run `pnpm typecheck` and `pnpm lint`.
- Run relevant tests (`pnpm --filter api test`, package tests).
- Report commands that could not run.

## Never

- Disable strict TS/ESLint or bypass auth guards (Clerk, `UlbApiKeyGuard`, print HMAC tokens) to compile.
- Create `middleware.ts` in web (use `proxy.ts`).
- Import `apps/*` from `packages/*`.
- Use `new PrismaClient()` — use `PrismaService` / `@workspace/database`.
- Put Prisma or secrets in `apps/web`.
- Call `@aws-sdk/*` from feature services — use `StorageService` / worker storage.
- Invent BullMQ names — use `@workspace/jobs`.
- Add npm dependencies without justification.
- Commit `.env` or secrets.
- Modify Docker/deployment without being asked.
- Make destructive changes without explicit instruction.

## Ask before

- New packages or module restructuring.
- Auth guard chain or permission model changes.
- Prisma schema / migrations.
- Docker, CI, or production config changes.
- New global Nest providers/interceptors.

## Next.js 16

Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` for unfamiliar APIs. Params are async. `proxy.ts` replaces `middleware.ts`.
